WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.078 --> 00:00:04.188
It was the day of the winter science fair.

2
00:00:04.189 --> 00:00:08.238
Stella sat at a table with a jar of snow.

3
00:00:08.239 --> 00:00:12.877
There was a display with information about snowflakes behind her.

4
00:00:12.878 --> 00:00:16.093
Her friend's mom came over to the table.

5
00:00:16.094 --> 00:00:19.329
"Hey, Stella. What's your project about?"

6
00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:25.636
Stella smiled. "Hi, Mrs. Singer. I did some research on snow."

7
00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:29.689
"That sounds interesting," Mrs. Singer said.

8
00:00:29.690 --> 00:00:33.677
"So, are you a snow expert now?"

9
00:00:33.678 --> 00:00:37.043
Stella grinned. "I'm not sure yet.

10
00:00:37.044 --> 00:00:39.880
But I learned how snow forms."

11
00:00:39.881 --> 00:00:44.050
By now a couple of other adults stood nearby.

12
00:00:44.051 --> 00:00:47.408
"Let's hear about it," the man said.

13
00:00:47.409 --> 00:00:50.131
"Okay," Stella said.

14
00:00:50.132 --> 00:00:55.737
"First the outdoor temperature must be 0 degrees Celsius or below.

15
00:00:55.738 --> 00:00:59.054
That freezes the water vapor in the air.

16
00:00:59.055 --> 00:01:04.296
The frozen vapor then attaches to specks of dust and pollen.

17
00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:07.886
When this happens, tiny ice crystals form.

18
00:01:07.887 --> 00:01:14.030
Like all crystals, these have flat sides and sharp corners.

19
00:01:14.031 --> 00:01:19.134
"Some of the ice crystals stick together, forming clumps of crystals.

20
00:01:19.135 --> 00:01:21.712
They grow bigger and bigger.

21
00:01:21.713 --> 00:01:27.029
Eventually all these crystals fall to the ground as snow."

22
00:01:27.030 --> 00:01:30.937
"Hmm." Mrs. Singer rubbed her chin.

23
00:01:30.938 --> 00:01:36.819
"So, snowflakes are just clumps of ice crystals that are stuck together?"

24
00:01:36.820 --> 00:01:43.195
Stella nodded. "Some snowflakes have up to two hundred ice crystals."

25
00:01:43.196 --> 00:01:45.745
"Whoa!" the woman said.

26
00:01:45.746 --> 00:01:49.804
"Can you tell us what makes the ice crystals fall out of the clouds?"

27
00:01:49.805 --> 00:01:56.096
"Yes," Stella said. "But the ice crystals don't really fall out of the clouds.

28
00:01:56.097 --> 00:01:59.320
The ice crystals are the clouds.

29
00:01:59.321 --> 00:02:01.840
They are what clouds are made of. "

30
00:02:01.841 --> 00:02:04.325
"Oh," the woman said.

31
00:02:04.326 --> 00:02:08.610
"The bunches of ice crystals get heavy," Stella said.

32
00:02:08.611 --> 00:02:11.398
"That's when they fall to the ground as snow.

33
00:02:11.399 --> 00:02:13.581
It's the same thing with rain.

34
00:02:13.582 --> 00:02:16.761
Water vapor turns into water droplets.

35
00:02:16.762 --> 00:02:18.577
They join together.

36
00:02:18.578 --> 00:02:23.678
And when the droplets are heavy enough, they fall as rain."

37
00:02:23.679 --> 00:02:26.735
Mrs. Singer pointed to the poster.

38
00:02:26.736 --> 00:02:30.720
"Tell us about those pretty snowflakes."

39
00:02:30.721 --> 00:02:36.287
"Sure." Stella stood up so everyone could see the poster better.

40
00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:40.657
"My poster shows all the basic shapes of snowflakes.

41
00:02:40.658 --> 00:02:44.599
Some are shaped like stars, needles, or plates.

42
00:02:44.600 --> 00:02:47.117
Others have little branches.

43
00:02:47.118 --> 00:02:51.126
Most snowflakes have six sides or six points.

44
00:02:51.127 --> 00:02:53.945
But every snowflake is different.

45
00:02:53.946 --> 00:02:59.091
In fact, you'll probably never find two that are exactly the same."

46
00:02:59.092 --> 00:03:03.799
"Huh," the man said. "Why are they all so different?"

47
00:03:03.800 --> 00:03:09.431
"Because ice crystals stick together in lots of different ways," Stella said.

48
00:03:09.432 --> 00:03:17.123
"Other things affect their shape too—like the air's temperature and its moisture levels.

49
00:03:17.124 --> 00:03:23.137
When there's just a little moisture in the air, snowflakes are shaped like flat plates.

50
00:03:23.138 --> 00:03:27.821
They're shaped like stars when there's more moisture in the air."

51
00:03:27.822 --> 00:03:33.009
"Very interesting!" the man said. "I never knew that."

52
00:03:33.010 --> 00:03:35.773
"Oh!" Stella said suddenly.

53
00:03:35.774 --> 00:03:38.160
"I just remembered one other thing.

54
00:03:38.161 --> 00:03:40.573
You know how snow looks white?

55
00:03:40.574 --> 00:03:45.462
Well, that's only because of how light reflects off all the crystals.

56
00:03:45.463 --> 00:03:48.343
Snow is actually clear."

57
00:03:48.344 --> 00:03:52.969
"Wow, Stella." Mrs. Singer smiled at her.

58
00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:56.093
"You are an expert on snow."

59
00:03:56.094 --> 00:03:59.850
"I guess I am." Stella smiled too.

60
00:03:59.851 --> 00:04:05.923
"To me, snowflakes are amazing!"

